e":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T00:40:57-07:00","id":646412,"title":"","content":"Ah, well then. Far less critical to get the Translation guide/ It's good, but not necessary. I liked it especially for the extra Form components. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T05:08:03-07:00","id":649969,"title":"","content":"Found an annoying bug that caused duplicate Exploits - Fixed. Found a more annoying bug that caused one chosen Exploit to be '56' - Fixed.<br /> <br /> &gt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> I've also made it very very slightly more user friendly by making the most basic GUI in the world - a window with a button. So now you can keep clicking the button to keep making new Demons to your heart's content.<br /> <br /> I've started working on generating Stats and Skills too. What do you think about the possibility of a Demon having a power that uses a Stat+Skill combination with a Stat of 1 and a Skill of 0? Is that acceptable? Unacceptable? Somewhere in between?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T15:07:06-07:00","id":650616,"title":"","content":"Strictly speaking, Embeds don't have skill or attribute prerequisites. <i>Why</i> a Demon would take the effort to learn something they wouldn't be good at is a question, but they aren't prevented. Note: That unskilled penalties <i>don't</i> apply, so the least they'll roll is a 1 (before modifiers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-03-2015, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-03T18:26:21-07:00","id":650829,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Embeds don't have the unskilled penalty so unless you've got negative modifiers applying you'll never hit that chance die. Sure, it won't be a <i>good</i> pool, but hey. But it might be worth weighting Embeds/Exploits to the attribute/skills present on the Demon to some degree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T00:27:08-07:00","id":650972,"title":"","content":"ok. I have weighted things slightly. Every Stat and Skill mentioned in the Form and known Embeds and Exploits now has a slightly higher chance of being assigned a dot. The more something is mentioned the higher the chance becomes, but it's never a certainty.<br /> <br /> I've uploaded a new release - fixes a couple of irritating bugs, too. 1. If only one embed is chosen, no exploits are chosen. 2. Only writes to the text file once per run of the program.<br /> <br /> So (touch wood), it's now in a good and usable state, ready for phase 2 - features.<br /> <br /> I'm open to requests!<br /> <br /> Things I want to add:<br /> 1. Display the stats and skills nicely.<br /> 2. GUI based user alteration of Form component amounts (rather than having to directly mod the ini file)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><b